 -direction-tblr dp-text-bold dp-border-style-solid dp-border-dir-tblr" sty
 le="border-width: 0px 2px 0px 0px\; padding-right: 12px\; background-color
 : #005a38\; color: #ffffff\;">Orientation</span> <span class="dp-header-ti
 tle dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr" style="margin-top:
  0px\; background-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\;">Honorlock Practice an
 d AI Agreement Quiz (Proctored)</span></h2>\n</header>\n<div class="dp-con
 tent-block lead dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-bord
 er-style-solid dp-border-dir-all dp-shadow-b1" style="margin: 50px 70px 40
 px\; padding: 25px 35px\; background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; bor
 der-width: 3px\; border-color: #005a38\;">\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">In th
 is activity\, you will review the course AI policy and set up Honorlock fo
 r proctored exams. You will then complete a short practice quiz that inclu
 des a reflection on the AI policy.</p>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-blo
 ck dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-shadow-b1 dp-bord
 er-dir-none" style="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 0px 35px 25px\; back
 ground-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; borde
 r-color: #005a38\;">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon dp-border-dir-tblr dp-border-
 style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="bor
 der-width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; padding-top: 
 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35px 30px\; f
 ont-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;"><span><strong>Purpose of the
  Quiz</strong></span></h3>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">This quiz serves two 
 purposes: to help you become familiar with the online proctoring process a
 nd to confirm your understanding of the course AI policy.</p>\n<p class="i
 sSelectedEnd">Before continuing in the course\, review the AI policy below
 \, complete the Honorlock setup\, and submit the quiz. Doing this now will
  help you prepare for your first proctored exam and avoid technical proble
 ms later.</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">The quiz includes a short reflecti
 on on the AI policy. Your response will also provide an example of your na
 tural writing style\, which may be helpful if an AI detector produces a fa
 lse positive in the future. Write in the same voice and style you would no
 rmally use for a paper in this course.</p>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content
 -block dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-shadow-b1 dp-
 border-dir-none" style="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 0px 35px 25px\; 
 background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; b
 order-color: #005a38\;">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon dp-border-dir-tblr dp-bor
 der-style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style=
 "border-width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; padding-t
 op: 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35px 30px
 \; font-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;"><strong>Read the AI Poli
 cy</strong></h3>\n<p><span>Artificial Intelligence can be useful in a host
  of situations\, but not in&nbsp\;<strong>any</strong>&nbsp\;assignments a
 nd papers for this course unless explicitly stated. I know other courses m
 ay encourage you to use AI\, but remember\, your&nbsp\;<strong>HUMANities&
 nbsp\;</strong>class needs to be 100%&nbsp\;<strong>HUMAN<em>.</em></stron
 g></span></p>\n<h4 class="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-te
 xt-bold" style="margin-top: 50px\; font-size: 20px\; margin-bottom: 10px\;
  color: #005a38\;">Develop Critical Thinking Skills</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr
 -solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-color: #eeeeee\; colo
 r: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 20px\;">\n<p><span>The purpo
 se of IHUM 201 is to develop critical thinking skills as you work your way
  through ideas in your own head\, gain new insights as you encounter new i
 deas\, discuss what you're learning about with others\, and come to your o
 wn conclusions. You need to write about those conclusions in your own voic
 e. Do not be tempted to delegate your&nbsp\;<strong>thinking or writing</s
 trong>&nbsp\;to AI. ChatGPT\, Gemini\, Grammarly\, CoPilot\, and the growi
 ng list cannot be used to write any part of your assignments and papers. N
 ot only is it academically dishonest to pass off AI-generated ideas and te
 xt as your own\, but the AI bot that generates that text creates a pretty 
 soulless product. It will simplify your complex ideas in the name of clari
 ty and tone.</span></p>\n<h4 class="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-pri
 mary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 50px\; font-size: 20px\; margin-bott
 om: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Blessed with a Unique Mind and Voice</h4>\n<h
 r class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-color: 
 #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 20px\;">\n<p><
 span>You—yes\, human you—are blessed with a unique\, individual mind a
 nd a unique\, individual voice. Believe in your ability to use both. I gen
 uinely want to hear what human you has to say. If you are worried about yo
 ur grammar\, spelling\, organization\, etc\, DO NOT run your writing throu
 gh AI. DO NOT ask any AI to write your outline or build your thesis. Talk 
 with a friend\, family member\, or classmate. Visit the&nbsp\;<a class="ex
 ternal" href="https://rwc.byu.edu/" target="_blank">BYU Writing and Resear
 ch Center<span class="external_link_icon" role="presentation"><span class=
 "screenreader-only">Links to an external site.</span></span></a>&nbsp\;eit
 her in person or virtually. Set up a meeting with your TA to go over your 
 writing. Read your writing out loud to hear what it actually sounds like. 
 Your skills will improve with your effort\, but they will not improve if A
 I does these things for you.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><span>For all writing i
 n this class\, you may use on the basic spell and grammar check in Microso
 ft Word\, Google Docs\, or in your web browser.&nbsp\;<strong>TURN OFF&nbs
 p\;</strong>Grammarly plugins or any similar extensions\, which will most 
 likely result in your work being flagged for AI use.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p
 ><span>If English is your second language\, again\, DO NOT run your work&n
 bsp\;through&nbsp\;AI checkers. To be accepted at BYU\, you had to show a 
 level of English proficiency&nbsp\;through&nbsp\;exams such as the TOEFL. 
 Your English language skills will only improve through practice\, not thro
 ugh AI&nbsp\;"fixing" your writing. Please utilize the resources mentioned
  above\, and\, if you feel it's necessary\, reach out to your TA to let th
 em know that English is not your primary language. We will take that into 
 account when grading your assignments and papers and give helpful feedback
  to improve your&nbsp\;</span><span>language skills.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<b
 lockquote class="dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="margin: 20px 45px\; bord
 er-left-color: #f1c232\;">\n<p class="">If an assignment or paper is flagg
 ed for containing any AI-generated text\, that assignment or paper will re
 ceive a zero. Your TA or I will reach out to in an email to let you know t
 hat your work has been flagged so we can talk about why it was flagged and
  whether or not you adhered to the above AI policy. Submitting a second as
 signment or paper that gets flagged for AI use is cause for dismissal from
  the class\, a failing grade\, and the need for a meeting with the Honor C
 ode Office to learn more about academic honesty.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p>\n</bloc
 kquote>\n<p><span>If you cannot commit to not using AI in all assignments 
 (unless explicitly stated)\, this course isn't for you!&nbsp\;</span></p>
 \n<p><span>This AI policy is based on the BYU Comparative Arts and Letters
  Position on AI. We recommend you familiarize yourself with it as well.&nb
 sp\;</span></p>\n<div class="dp-panels-wrapper dp-accordion-default">\n<di
 v class="dp-panel-group">\n<h3 class="dp-panel-heading">BYU Comparative Ar
 ts and Letters Position on AI</h3>\n<div class="dp-panel-content">\n<h4 cl
 ass="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margi
 n-top: 20px\; font-size: 18px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Pr
 actice</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style=
 "border-color: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom:
  20px\;">\n<p><span><i>AI and LLMs in the&nbsp\; BYU Comparative Arts &amp
 \; Letters Classroom</i></span></p>\n<p><span>You won’t find the same AI
  policies in a humanities class as what you may encounter in other fields 
 across campus. Reading\, writing\, brainstorming\, editing\, visualizing\,
  creating\, and analyzing texts and artworks are crucial enterprises that 
 should not be offloaded without clear-eyed deliberation about their effect
 s (in all realms - cognitive\, ethical\, social\, aesthetic\, spiritual\, 
 etc.). Pay attention to each of your instructor’s policies and be ready 
 to commit to humanistic work in its richness and rigor. As a peculiar peop
 le\, we should not be afraid to go against the cultural grain--to go slowe
 r when the world demands we speed up\; to savor instead of consume\; to qu
 estion\, rather than prompt\; to listen more deeply rather than scroll mor
 e voraciously\; to painstakingly craft rather than reproduce or simulate. 
 We understand the inseparable relationships of culture and technology\, ma
 teriality and media\, and believe that ongoing experience and spiritual di
 scernment are vital to navigating those relationships in our teaching\, re
 search\, and spiritual mission. As Latter-day Saint humanists we believe e
 ducation is aimed at nothing less than building the kingdom for the glory 
 of God\, whose glory is not artificial\, but authentic and embodied loving
  intelligence.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<div><span>&nbsp\;</span></div>\n
 <h4 class="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style=
 "margin-top: 20px\; font-size: 18px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38
 \;">Principles</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr
 " style="border-color: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin
 -bottom: 20px\;">\n<p><span><i>On the importance of being human(ists)</i><
 /span></p>\n<p><span>Our understanding of the humanities as Latter-day Sai
 nts recognizes embodied experience as the central purpose of our mortal jo
 urney. The humanities are an exploration of mortal experience: of the hist
 orical and cultural forces that shape us and confront us as human beings\,
  and which provoke innumerable forms of human expressions and responses ov
 er time and across space. These expressions and responses in their varied 
 forms are the humanist’s objects of study. In the humanities\, form\, co
 ntent\, and context are interconnected in the process of making meaning\, 
 in contrast to other disciplines which may regard objects primarily in ter
 ms of the content they convey or their perceived utility. In addition\, th
 e kinds of cognitive offloading and deskilling that these technologies app
 ear to foster run counter to many of the goals of a BYU education and to o
 ur shared mortal purpose of gaining experience and intelligence through li
 ved experience.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><span><i>On “generative” technol
 ogies</i></span></p>\n<p><span>Technologies that purport to generate langu
 age at unprecedented scale and speed obscure the practices that backstop t
 hose technologies (some of which are ethically and morally dubious)\; they
  also make the practice of writing (and writing-as-thinking) seem trivial 
 and automatable. All of this is of great concern to us as Latter-Day Saint
  humanists. We view large language models (chatbots\, LLMs\, “AI”)&nbs
 p\; not as neutral or transparent tools of information\, but products of c
 ultural and corporate ideologies that must be the objects of study rather 
 than means of outsourcing creativity and analysis. Any use of AI in the hu
 manities is necessarily an exercise in critical thinking\, not simply a me
 ans of transmission.</span></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-ca
 llout dp-callout-placeholder card dp-callout-position-default dp-callout-t
 ype-default dp-callout-color-dp-primary dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="m
 argin-top: 40px\; margin-bottom: 15px\; background-color: #e2eee9\; color:
  #000000\; border-radius: 6px\; border: 1px solid #005a38\;">\n<div class=
 "card-body" style="padding: 18px 22px\;">\n<h4 class="card-title" style="c
 olor: #005a38\; margin-top: 0px\;">Academic Integrity</h4>\n<p><span>Pleas
 e carefully review the following information regarding academic integrity.
 </span></p>\n<p><span>By accessing BYU Online academic exams\, you acknowl
 edge that you have read and understand the BYU Academic Honesty Policy. <s
 trong>For clarity\, we want to remind you that the BYU Academic Honesty Po
 licy and all related policies apply to you when you take this test or quiz
 \, and we want to check your recognition of this fact. </strong>You agree 
 to uphold the principles of academic honesty and integrity\, follow all ex
 am rules and guidelines (including the use of proctoring services)\, and a
 dhere to the consequences of any violations as outlined in the BYU Academi
 c Honesty Policy. <strong>Please note that you must agree to each requirem
 ent in this quiz to proceed with this course</strong></span></p>\n</div>\n
 </div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-p
 adding-direction-tblr dp-shadow-b1 dp-border-dir-none" style="margin: 50px
  70px 40px\; padding: 0px 35px 25px\; background-color: #ffffff\; color: #
 000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; border-color: #005a38\;">\n<h3 class=
 "dp-has-icon dp-border-dir-tblr dp-border-style-solid dp-padding-direction
 -tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-width: 0px\; padding-left: 2
 2px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; padding-top: 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; c
 olor: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35px 30px\; font-size: 24px\; background-colo
 r: #005a38\;"><strong>Honorlock</strong><strong></strong></h3>\n<p><span><
 a class="dp-import-page" href="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/10881/p
 ages/exam-instructions?module_item_id=2232810" data-api-endpoint="https://
 byu.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/10881/pages/exam-instructions" data-api
 -returntype="Page">Preparing for Your Exam</a></span></p>\n<div class="dp-
 embed-wrapper" data-ratio-w="37.07" data-ratio-h="0.03"></div>\n</div>\n<d
 iv class="dp-content-block dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-t
 blr" style="padding: 20px 25px\; background-color: #005a38\; color: #fffff
 f\; margin-top: 55px\; margin-bottom: 0px\;">\n<div class="dp-progress-pla
 ceholder dp-module-progress-completion dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="di
 splay: none\; background-color: #eeeeee\; color: #000000\;">Module Item Co
 mpletion (browser only)</div>\n</div>\n</div><script src="https://instruct
