 ncepts to study so you are better prepared for the concepts covered in the
  upcoming exams.\n\nInstructions\n------------\n\nThis multiple-choice qui
 z draws from a large question bank\, so each attempt may include questions
  you have not seen before.\n\nTo prepare\, review:\n\n* Learning Outcomes 
 on the overview page\n\n* The “Terms to Track” and “People to Track
 ” sections at the lesson pages\n\nYou may retake the quiz as many times 
 as needed. For the best preparation\, continue taking it until you have en
 countered every question in the question bank. Unit Checks draw from a sim
 ilar bank\, so the more questions you encounter and review now\, the bette
 r prepared you will be.\n\nRules\n-----\n\nThe quiz consists of the follow
 ing rules.\n\n* Open book and note (so you can know what concepts to focus
  on for the exams)\n\n* Unlimited attempts\n\n* No time limit\n\n* Your hi
 ghest score will be kept\n\nIf taking this quiz again after the due date\,
  use the practice quiz below.\n\nUsing the Quiz for Exam Review\n---------
 ---------------------\n\nAfter the due date\, use [Mini-Concept Check: Ear
 ly Greece and Epic Poetry (Practice)] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses
 /36390/quizzes/656510) to review for the exam. It contains the same questi
 ons and can be taken late without affecting this score. No points are asso
 ciated with the practice version of this quiz.\n\nModule Item Completion (
 browser only)
