BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start the Intellectual Virtue Project [IHUM 201-022]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTSTAMP:20260903T150800Z
UID:event-assignment-1466320
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:--------------------------------------------------\nOrientatio
 n Start the Intellectual Virtue Project\n---------------------------------
 -----------------\n\nAs you hopefully read earlier in this lesson\, you wi
 ll have one course-long project that will culminate in a final synthesis p
 aper. This is the beginning of that assignment. On this page\, you will re
 ad about nine intellectual virtues and select one to cultivate in your own
  life and to use as a lens to analyze culture and history of the Western w
 orld from ancient history to the High Renaissance.  \n\nContext\n-------
 \n\nThroughout time\, people have asked the same question: How do I live a
  good life?\n\nAs a student right now\, you might be thinking something si
 milar: Will what I’m doing now help me live a good life? How do I live a
  good life in the present\, and how do I build a good life for the future?
  What will bring true happiness\, fulfillment\, and meaning to my life?\n
 \nThroughout this course\, we will be looking at the many different ways W
 estern civilization has dealt with these questions. To assist you in your 
 understanding of these questions and ideas\, both past and present\, and t
 o help you find an overarching and personalized theme to this course\, we 
 are going to start by learning about intellectual virtues and selecting a 
 specific intellectual virtue you would like to practice during your time i
 n IHUM 201.  \n\nLearn About Virtues\n-------------------\n\nIntroduction
  to the Chapter\n---------------------------\n\nYou’ll notice that the c
 hapter you will read is from a book primarily directed at instructors. How
 ever\, the information is pertinent to students or anyone who wants to be 
 in charge of his or her own learning\, not just in school\, but throughout
  life. After some introduction\, Baehr will present nine key intellectual 
 virtues:\n\n* Curiosity\n\n* Autonomy\n\n* Humility\n\n* Attentiveness\n\n
 * Carefulness\n\n* Thoroughness\n\n* Open-mindedness\n\n* Courage\n\n* Ten
 acity \n\nAs you read\, pay special attention to which virtue excites you
 \, interests you\, or that you feel could really help you. Take notes on w
 hat it is that specifically stands out to you about that virtue. \n\nWhic
 hever virtue you choose\, you will focus on throughout the course. You wil
 l search for this virtue\, or lack of it\, in what you learn each week\, i
 n addition to working to build it in your own life.\n\n​\n\nCome Closer 
 to Christ\n---------------------\n\nEach of these virtues reflects an attr
 ibute of Jesus Christ. As you cultivate one throughout the semester\, you 
 can become more like Him.\n\nStudying people from the past with humility a
 nd charity can also help you see them as Christ does. Consider how your ch
 osen virtue can deepen both your learning and your discipleship.\n\nRead a
 nd Annotate the Chapter\n-----------------------------\n\nStep 1: Download
  Chapter 2 (pages 31-49) from Jason Baehr’s Deep in Thought book.\n\nSte
 p 2: Upload the chapter to your favorite tool that can highlight and add a
 nnotations in the margins.\n\nStep 3: As you read\, annotate by highlighti
 ng and taking notes in the margins about the different virtues. You will s
 ubmit your annotated PDF along with your write-up. \n\nExternal Reading\n
 \nDeep in Thought (Chapter 2)\n\nLog in to the BYU library with your NetID
  to access the reading\n\n[Open Chapter →] (https://ebookcentral.proques
 t.com/lib/byu/detail.action?docID=7263089)\n\nChoose and Reflect\n--------
 ----------\n\nFor this writing assignment\, you will write three thoughtfu
 l paragraphs discussing your reaction to and insights about the nine key v
 irtues.  \n\nYou will be graded on how thoroughly and thoughtfully you an
 swer each question and how clearly you organize and communicate your ideas
 . Minor writing errors will not affect your score unless they make your re
 sponse difficult to understand.\n\nParagraph #1\n------------\n\nWrite abo
 ut your “top three” virtues by answering the following questions.\n\n*
 \n\n* Why do these three virtues interest you the most?\n\n* Does Baehr ex
 plain a virtue in a way you hadn’t thought about it before?\n\n* Have yo
 u noticed a particular virtue in someone else that makes you want to work 
 on it?  \n\nParagraph #2\n------------\n\nNarrow in on the specific virtu
 e you want to practice throughout this class. Talk about it in more detail
  than you did in the first paragraph.\n\n*\n\n* What is it about this virt
 ue that most appeals to you?\n\n* Why do you want to specifically work on 
 this virtue as opposed to the others in your top three?\n\nParagraph #3\n-
 -----------\n\nI understand that this is the beginning of the course\, so 
 you do not yet know everything we will be studying. Therefore\, this next 
 question is meant to be a conjecture.\n\n*\n\n* How do you think or expect
  you could look for this virtue in art\, architecture\, music\, philosophy
 \, and literature?\n\nIt will be interesting at the end of the course to l
 ook back and see where you actually saw the virtue in practice and what yo
 u learned about the virtue from the past and your own implementation of it
 .  \n\nWhat to Submit\n--------------\n\nYou will submit two files on thi
 s page.\n\n* Annotated PDF of Chapter 2 (with highlights and notes in the 
 margins)\n\n* Your three paragraphs as a DOCX or PDF file\n\nReview the ru
 bric below before you submit. The rubric will walk you through what the TA
 s will look for when grading. \n\n​\n\nWhat should I do next?\n--------
 --------------\n\nComplete the following steps throughout this course.\n\n
 * Take note of when you see the virtue\, or lack of it\, in the lesson mat
 erial\n\n* Submit your notes periodically in a Deep Dive Report (about onc
 e a week)\n\n* Share one way you are cultivating the virtue in your life i
 n the same Deep Dive Report (about once a week)\n\nThis project will culmi
 nate at the end of the course in you presenting your findings on what you 
 learned about the chosen virtue from history and your personal life.\n\nMo
 dule Item Completion (browser only)
