DESCRIPTION:--------------------------------------------------\nLesson 2 T
 he Iliad Project (Part 1) - Annotations\n---------------------------------
 -----------------\n\nIn this part of the project\, you’ll highlight epit
 hets\, take notes on attributes of Achilles and Hector\, and document cult
 ural ideals. This part of the project must be submitted in order to receiv
 e point on the written portion in Part 2. The annotation must be your own 
 work. \n\nHighlight and Take Notes\n------------------------\n\nThis comp
 rises the steps for Part 1 of your project.\n\nPlease download a copy of t
 he [Iliad Selections PDF] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/36390/files
 /13583108?wrap=1). \n\nWhat to Highlight\n-----------------\n\nIn your PD
 F copy of the Iliad selections (and without the assistance of any kind of 
 AI)\, highlight any epic epithet you encounter for the following major cha
 racters: Achilles\, Agamemnon\, Hector\, Paris\, Helen\, Andromache\, Pria
 m\, Zeus\, Hera\, Athena\, Apollo\, Aphrodite\, Thetis\, and Hephaestus.\n
 \nUse these colors:\n\n* Yellow: Achilles\n\n* Green: Hector\n\n* Blue: Al
 l other characters\n\nNoticing these epithets will help you gain a better 
 grasp of the ideal characteristics of Greek culture\, as they tell us how 
 we are supposed to visualize and imagine these heroes and gods. \n\nWhat 
 to Take Notes On\n---------------------\n\nAs you read\, look beyond the e
 pithets and take notes in the margins of your PDF copy of the Iliad select
 ions on two additional areas (use different highlight colors from the ones
  you used for the epithets). This may sound like a broken record\, but thi
 s also must be done without the assistance of any AI. This is how you--bri
 lliant\, capable human you-- engages with a text. \n\n*\n\nAchilles and H
 ector: Take note in the margins or highlight what each hero's defining att
 ributes are. These should be based on the characters’ words or actions\,
  not their epithets. Pay special attention to evidence that could help you
  decide which hero best represents areté. You will document and write abo
 ut this in Part 2.\n\n*\n\nGreek cultural ideals: Take notes in the margin
 s on the cultural ideals you notice and highlight specific examples from t
 he text. You will write about this in Part 2.\n\nWhat to Submit\n---------
 -----\n\nYou will submit two items on this page\n\n* Your annotated select
 ions from the Iliad (highlights and notes in the margins). Submit this as 
 a PDF file.\n\n* Statement in the submission comment box saying\, "This is
  all my own work\, and I didn't use AI."\n\n* If this statement is not tru
 e\, please redo this assignment using your own work before you submit it.
 \n\n* If this statement is not included in the submission comment\, the as
 signment will not be graded.\n\nRemember\, the annotation must be your own
  work. If you submit a PDF of someone else's work\, that is plagiarism. If
  you use AI in any way to annotate your text\, that is academic dishonesty
 . Both will be reported to the Honor Code Office and will result in a zero
  grade on the entire project. \n\nNote: You must submit your annotations 
 before Part 2 of the Iliad Project (the worksheet) will be graded.\n\nModu
 le Item Completion (browser only)
