 fffff\;">\n<h2 class="dp-heading dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direc
 tion-tblr" style="margin-top: 0px\; margin-bottom: 0px\; padding-bottom: 2
 0px\; padding-top: 18px\; padding-left: 5px\; border-color: #2b4226\; colo
 r: #ffffff\;">\n<span class="dp-header-pre dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-ma
 rgin-direction-tblr dp-text-bold dp-border-style-solid dp-border-dir-tblr"
  style="border-width: 0px 2px 0px 0px\; padding-right: 12px\; background-c
 olor: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\;"> <span class="dp-header-pre-1" style="co
 lor: #ffffff\;">Lesson 2</span> </span> <span class="dp-header-title dp-ma
 rgin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr" style="margin-top: 0px\;">T
 he Iliad Project (Part 1) - Annotations</span>\n</h2>\n</header>\n<div cla
 ss="dp-content-block dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp
 -border-style-solid dp-border-dir-all dp-shadow-b1" style="margin: 50px 70
 px 40px\; padding: 25px 35px\; background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000
 \; border-width: 3px\; border-color: #005A38\;">\n<p class="lead">In this 
 part of the project\, you’ll highlight epithets\, take notes on attribut
 es of Achilles and Hector\, and document cultural ideals. This part of the
  project must be submitted in order to receive point on the written portio
 n in Part 2. The annotation must be your own work.&nbsp\;</p>\n</div>\n<di
 v class="dp-content-block dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tb
 lr dp-shadow-b1 dp-border-dir-none" style="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; paddin
 g: 0px 35px 25px\; background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-wid
 th: 5px 0px 0px\; border-color: #005A38\;">\n<h3 class="dp-border-dir-tblr
  dp-border-style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr"
  style="border-width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; pa
 dding-top: 12px\; border-color: #005A38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -40
 px 30px\; font-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;">\n<strong>Highlig
 ht and Take Notes</strong><strong></strong>\n</h3>\n<p>This comprises the 
 steps for Part 1 of your project.</p>\n<p>Please download a copy of the <a
  class="instructure_file_link instructure_scribd_file inline_disabled" hre
 f="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/36390/files/13583108?wrap=1" target
 ="_blank" data-canvas-previewable="true" data-api-endpoint="https://byu.in
 structure.com/api/v1/courses/36390/files/13583108" data-api-returntype="Fi
 le">Iliad Selections PDF</a>.&nbsp\;</p>\n<h4 class="dp-margin-direction-t
 blr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 40px\; font-size: 2
 2px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">What to Highlight</h4>\n<hr 
 class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-color: #e
 eeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 15px\;">\n<p>In 
 your PDF copy of the <em>Iliad</em> selections (and without the assistance
  of any kind of AI)\, highlight any epic epithet you encounter for the fol
 lowing major characters: Achilles\, Agamemnon\, Hector\, Paris\, Helen\, A
 ndromache\, Priam\, Zeus\, Hera\, Athena\, Apollo\, Aphrodite\, Thetis\, a
 nd Hephaestus.</p>\n<p>Use these colors:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<span style="bac
 kground-color: #fbeeb8\;">Yellow:</span> Achilles</li>\n<li>\n<span style=
 "background-color: #bfedd2\;">Green:</span> Hector</li>\n<li>\n<span style
 ="background-color: #c2e0f4\;">Blue:</span> All other characters</li>\n</u
 l>\n<p>Noticing these epithets will help you gain a better grasp of the id
 eal characteristics of Greek culture\, as they tell us how we are supposed
  to visualize and imagine these heroes and gods.&nbsp\;</p>\n<h4 class="dp
 -margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 
 40px\; font-size: 22px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">What to T
 ake Notes On</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" 
 style="border-color: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-b
 ottom: 15px\;">\n<p>As you read\, look beyond the epithets and take notes 
 in the margins of your PDF copy of the Iliad selections on two additional 
 areas (use different highlight colors from the ones you used for the epith
 ets). This may sound like a broken record\, but this also must be done wit
 hout the assistance of any AI. This is how you--brilliant\, capable human 
 you-- engages with a text.&nbsp\;</p>\n<ol start="1">\n<li>\n<p class="dp-
 margin-direction-tblr" style="margin-bottom: 5px\;"><strong>Achilles and H
 ector:</strong> Take note in the margins or highlight what each hero's def
 ining attributes are. These should be based on the characters’ words or 
 actions\, not their epithets. Pay special attention to evidence that could
  help you decide which hero best represents areté. You will document and 
 write about this in Part 2.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Greek cultural id
 eals:</strong> Take notes in the margins on the cultural ideals you notice
  and highlight specific examples from the text. You will write about this 
 in Part 2.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block dp-marg
 in-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-shadow-b1 dp-border-dir-non
 e" style="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 0px 35px 25px\; background-col
 or: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; border-color: #
 005A38\;">\n<h3 class="dp-border-dir-tblr dp-border-style-solid dp-padding
 -direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-width: 0px\; paddi
 ng-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; padding-top: 12px\; border-color: #
 005A38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -40px 30px\; font-size: 24px\; backg
 round-color: #005a38\;"><strong>What to Submit</strong></h3>\n<p>You will 
 submit two items on this page</p>\n<ol style="list-style-type: decimal\;">
 \n<li>Your annotated selections from the <em>Iliad</em> (highlights and no
 tes in the margins). Submit this as a PDF file.</li>\n<li>\n<span data-olk
 -copy-source="MessageBody">Statement in the submission comment box saying
 \, "This is all my own work\, and I didn't use AI." </span>\n<ul style="li
 st-style-type: disc\;">\n<li><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">If t
 his statement is not true\, please redo this assignment using your own wor
 k before you submit it. </span></li>\n<li><span data-olk-copy-source="Mess
 ageBody">If this statement is not included in the submission comment\, the
  assignment will not be graded.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Remem
 ber\, the annotation must be your own work. If you submit a PDF of someone
  else's work\, that is plagiarism. If you use AI in any way to annotate yo
 ur text\, that is academic dishonesty. Both will be reported to the Honor 
 Code Office and will result in a zero grade on the entire project.&nbsp\;<
 /p>\n<blockquote class="dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="background-color:
  #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-left-color: #f1c232\; margin-top: 25px
 \;">\n<p>Note: You must submit your annotations before Part 2 of the <em>I
 liad</em> Project (the worksheet) will be graded.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</di
 v>\n<div class="dp-content-block dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direc
