DESCRIPTION:------------------------------\nOrientation Introduce Yourself
 \n------------------------------\n\nIn this activity\, you will explore ho
 w a “second language” can come from an interest\, skill\, or community
 . Then you will introduce yourself in a short video and respond to two cla
 ssmates.\n\n​\n\nJoin a Group Before Posting\n--------------------------
 -\n\nEnsure you have completed the [Join a Group] (LINK.PLACEHOLDER_df2696
 e4db9fd57edfe986e674dfb95c) quiz before you post to this discussion board.
  If not\, your post will appear on the general board that none of your pee
 rs can see\, and you will be unable to see your peers' posts.\n\nRead Arti
 cle\n------------\n\nBefore you complete your post\, read the following tw
 o-page article from the BYU College of Humanities. Think about what one of
  your "second languages" could be. \n\n[What's Your Second Language?] (LI
 NK.PLACEHOLDER_a8fa98395f41259abc558210c8d21f9d)\n\nPost Video Response\n-
 ------------------\n\nRecord and post a 1–2 minute video for your small 
 group. Using the article’s idea of a “second language\," address the f
 ollowing.\n\n* Introduce yourself and name one “second language” you s
 peak.\n\n* Share a word\, phrase\, gesture\, or inside reference from that
  language. Explain what it means.\n\n* Tell how you learned this language.
 \n\n* Share how it shows who you are or helps you connect with others.\n\n
 Your second language could come from a hobby\, field of study\, culture\, 
 community\, fandom\, faith\, or other part of your life.\n\nHow do I recor
 d a video in my post?\n\nAfter you click Reply below\, complete the follow
 ing steps to record your video.\n\n[Click Upload/Record Media after clicki
 ng Reply. Don't Attach a video.] (LINK.PLACEHOLDER_b3b447133ff29b4dbec2f8a
 c39e2ab2d)     \n\n[Click on the Record button instead of uploading a f
 ile from the computer.] (LINK.PLACEHOLDER_dca70a6f64f2597768189192bd07f73d
 )     \n\n[Click the Start Recording button] (LINK.PLACEHOLDER_6c38d6e4
 2c979c53b0ab719367430c66)     \n\nSince your classmates are relying on 
 you to post on time so they can respond\, late posts will not be accepted.
  \n\nMake Two Comments\n-----------------\n\nWatch your group members’ 
 videos and leave a short\, written response for at least two classmates.\n
 \nIn each response:\n\n* Mention something specific from the video that ca
 ught your attention.\n\n* Share a brief reaction or personal connection.\n
 \nWrite 2–3 thoughtful and encouraging sentences.\n\nIn most careers\, y
 our work depends on others. Learning to wait\, plan ahead\, and follow thr
 ough is a valuable professional skill. Therefore\, if you post your main v
 ideo first or second\, set a reminder to return and respond after two peer
 s have posted.\n\nGrading\n-------\n\nClick on the     button in the t
 op right-hand corner to see the Rubric.\n\nModule Item Completion (browser
  only)
