SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:-----------------------------\nLesson 3 Greek Temple Sketch\n-
 ----------------------------\n\nSince we’re going to encounter a lot of 
 architecture throughout this class\, it’s time to become really familiar
  with some architectural terms. Greek architecture is the basis for centur
 ies and centuries of architecture that follow the fall of the Greek empire
 \, and it is still used in buildings today.\n\nBeing able to recognize and
  name parts of architecture will help you throughout the rest of this clas
 s and IHUM 202. It will also make looking at architecture in your everyday
  life more interesting. Sometimes a modern architect will hearken back to 
 Greek prototypes. Once you know the terminology\, you will more readily re
 cognize Greek architecture whenever you happen upon it.\n\nTerms to Track
 \n\nWatch for these terms as you read:\n\n all of the bolded terms you wi
 ll include in your architectural sketches\n\nArchitectural Terms\n--------
 -----------\n\n Go to this page and read the article about the Doric and 
 Ionic orders:\n\nExternal Reading\n\nDoric and Ionic Orders\n\n[Open Artic
 le →] (https://classicalarthistory.wordpress.com/2015/11/21/doric-and-io
 nic-orders/)\n\nHere is a great video that will walk you through the footp
 rint of a Greek temple and the elevations of both the Doric and Ionic orde
 rs. You can watch the whole video and then sketch or you can follow along 
 and pause as needed a while you create the sketch assignment described bel
 ow. You are also welcome to look up any terms if the vocabulary is unclear
 . \n\nTranscript: Forthcoming\n\nSketch a Greek Temple\n-----------------
 ----\n\nOne of the best ways to cement these terms in your memory is to ph
 ysically draw and label the parts of a Greek temple and the Doric and Ioni
 c orders.\n\nFor this assignment\, you are going to make three sketches. Y
 ou may do a pen/pencil and paper sketch\, or you may use a digital drawing
  program where you are actually drawing the image with a digital pen.\n\nA
 I-generated drawings are not allowed for this assignment.\n\n[Black-and-wh
 ite floor plan of the Temple of Hera showing the rectangular cella\, surro
 unding colonnade\, and internal rows of columns] (https://byu.instructure.
 com/courses/36390/files/13583104/download?download_frd=1&hidden=1) Plan of
  the Temple of Hera I at Paestum\n\nSketch 1: Temple Footprint Sketch\n---
 ------------------------------\n\nFirst\, sketch the basic footprint of a 
 [peripteral] (#dpPeripteralContent) temple\, such as the Temple of Hera yo
 u learned about earlier in the lesson. Label the following areas on your s
 ketch.\n\nA temple having a single row of columns around the cella and por
 ticos\, as opposed to a dipteral temple\, which has a double row of column
 s surrounding the central areas.\n\n* Cella or naos (also write what usual
 ly sits inside a naos)\n\n* Pronaos or portico\n\n* Opisthodomos or rear-f
 acing portico\n\n* Surrounding colonnade with an appropriate number of col
 umns for the different sides (remember what the articles and videos have s
 aid about the geometry of the temples)\n\nSketch 2 & 3: Doric and Ionic Te
 mple Elevations\n-----------------------------------------------\n\nNext\,
  sketch the elevations of the corners of a Doric order temple and an Ionic
  order temple from the stereobate to the raking cornice. This means you wi
 ll have two sketches: one of the Doric order and one of the Ionic order.\n
 \nOn your drawings\, label the following items.\n\n* Stereobate\n\n* Stylo
 bate\n\n* Column base (be sure to identify which order uses a base)\n\n* C
 olumn shaft\n\n* Capital (be sure to correctly identify which capital belo
 ngs to which order)\n\n* Entablature\n\n* Frieze\n\n* Architrave\n\n* Corn
 ice\n\n* Triglyph and Metope (this will only show up in the frieze of one 
 of the two orders\; make sure it’s the correct one)\n\n* Pediment\n\n* R
 aking cornice\n\nRemember\, you are doing one sketch for a Doric order tem
 ple and another for an Ionic order temple. \n\nWhat to Submit\n----------
 ----\n\nWhen you are done\, submit a photo(s) of your three sketches with 
 all parts labeled.\n\n* Temple Footprint\n\n* Doric Order Temple Elevation
 \n\n* Ionic Order Temple Elevation\n\nRemember\, you may use a pen/pencil 
 and paper or a digital drawing program with a digital pen. No AI-generated
  drawings are allowed for this assignment. That negates the retention bene
 fit you get from drawing and labeling by hand. \n\nModule Item Completion
  (browser only)\n\nAttributions\n\n* Plan of the Temple of Hera I at Paest
 um. Created by Xkx\, 2007. CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL. [Wikimedia Commons sourc
 e] (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pianta_hera_paestum.jpg).
