 \; margin: auto\; border-radius: 3px\; border: 1px solid #a9a9a9\;">\n<p>A
  temple having a single row of columns around the cella and porticos\, as 
 opposed to a dipteral temple\, which has a double row of columns surroundi
 ng the central areas.</p>\n</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Cella or <strong>naos</strong
 > (also write what usually sits inside a naos)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Pronaos
 </strong> or portico</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Opisthodomos</strong> or rear-fac
 ing portico</li>\n<li>Surrounding <strong>colonnade</strong> with an appro
 priate number of columns for the different sides (remember what the articl
 es and videos have said about the geometry of the temples)</li>\n</ul>\n<h
 4 id="architecture-as-inspiration" class="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-
 dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 50px\; font-size: 22px\; margi
 n-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Sketch 2 &amp\; 3: Doric and Ionic Temp
 le Elevations</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr"
  style="border-color: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\;">\n<p>N
 ext\, sketch the elevations of the corners of a Doric order temple and an 
 Ionic order temple from the stereobate to the raking cornice. This means y
 ou will have two sketches: one of the Doric order and one of the Ionic ord
 er.</p>\n<p>On your drawings\, label the following items.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><
 strong>Stereobate</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Stylobate</strong></li>\n<li>
 \n<strong>Column base</strong> (be sure to identify which order uses a bas
 e)</li>\n<li><strong>Column shaft</strong></li>\n<li>\n<strong>Capital</st
 rong> (be sure to correctly identify which capital belongs to which order)
 </li>\n<li>\n<strong>Entablature</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Frieze</stron
 g></li>\n<li><strong>Architrave</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Cornice</strong
 ></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Triglyph</strong> and <strong>Metope</
 strong> (this will only show up in the frieze of one of the two orders\; m
 ake sure it’s the correct one)</li>\n<li><strong>Pediment</strong></li>
 \n<li><strong>Raking cornice</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Remember\, you are d
 oing one sketch for a Doric order temple and another for an Ionic order te
 mple.&nbsp\;</p>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block dp-margin-direction
 -tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-shadow-b1 dp-border-dir-none" style="ma
 rgin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 0px 35px 25px\; background-color: #ffffff
 \; color: #000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; border-color: #005a38\;">
 \n<h3 id="greek-architectural-sketch" class="dp-border-dir-tblr dp-border-
 style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="bor
 der-width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; padding-top: 
 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35px 30px\; f
 ont-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;"><strong>What to Submit</stro
 ng></h3>\n<p>When you are done\, submit a photo(s) of your three sketches 
 with all parts labeled.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Temple Footprint</li>\n<li>Doric Or
 der Temple Elevation</li>\n<li>Ionic Order Temple Elevation</li>\n</ul>\n<
 blockquote class="dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="background-color: #ffff
 ff\; color: #000000\; margin-top: 25px\; border-left-color: #f1c232\;">\n<
 p>Remember\, you may use a pen/pencil and paper or a digital drawing progr
 am with a digital pen. <em>No AI-generated drawings</em> are allowed for t
 his assignment. That negates the retention benefit you get from drawing an
 d labeling by hand.&nbsp\;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-cont
 ent-block dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="paddi
 ng: 20px 25px\; background-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin-top: 5
 5px\; margin-bottom: 0px\;">\n<div class="dp-progress-placeholder dp-modul
 e-progress-completion dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="display: none\; bac
 kground-color: #eeeeee\; color: #000000\;">Module Item Completion (browser
  only)</div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block dp-padding-direction-tb
 lr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="padding-top: 20px\; background-color: 
 #ffffff\;"><details class="dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-t
 blr" style="margin: 0px 2px 40px\;">\n<summary class="dp-margin-direction-
 tblr" style="border-top: 1px solid #cccccc\; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc
 ccc\; padding: 10px 0px 10px 15px\; color: #005a38\; width: 100%\; font-si
 ze: 16pt\; margin-top: 30px\; margin-bottom: 15px\;"><span style="font-siz
 e: 18px\; color: #2d3b45\;">Attributions</span></summary>\n<div class="dp-
 margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr" style="padding: 0px 20px
 \;">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<em>Plan of the Temple of Hera I at Paestum</em>. Create
 d by Xkx\, 2007. CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL. <a href="https://commons.wikimedia
 .org/wiki/File:Pianta_hera_paestum.jpg" target="_blank">Wikimedia Commons 
 source</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</details></div>\n</div><script src="http
 s://instructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachm
 ents/8409019/dp_app.js"></script>
END:VEVENT
