BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Architecture Sighting or Sketch: Greek [IHUM 201-022]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260919
DTSTAMP:20260901T180800Z
UID:event-assignment-1466323
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:-----------------------------------------------\nLesson 4 Arch
 itecture Sighting or Sketch: Greek\n--------------------------------------
 ---------\n\nFind and identify Greek architectural features on a real buil
 ding. Choose one of the two options below.\n\nInstructions\n------------\n
 \nChoose one of the following ways to complete this assignment.\n\nOption 
 1: Visit a Building (preferred option)\n----------------------------------
 -----------\n\nStep 1: Find a Building\n-----------------------\n\nLook fo
 r a building with at least four Greek architectural elements from the list
  below.\n\nGood places to search include:\n\n* Universities\n\n* Governmen
 t buildings\n\n* Theaters\n\n* Banks\n\n* Museums\n\n* Libraries\n\nStep 2
 : Take a Photograph\n-------------------------\n\nTake a photograph that:
 \n\n* Shows you standing in front of the building\n\n* Clearly shows the a
 rchitectural elements you plan to identify\n\nSelfies are welcome\, but yo
 u need to be able to see the architectural element. Consider bringing a fr
 iend or family member and sharing what you've learned with them. They will
  be so impressed with your architectural knowledge. You may use a photogra
 ph from a previous trip or occasion\, but you must be in the photo. Findin
 g a building during the current term is encouraged!\n\nStep 3: Submit Your
  Work\n------------------------\n\nSubmit the following:\n\n* Your photogr
 aph\n\n* The building’s name and location\n\n* Four clearly identified G
 reek architectural elements visible in the photograph--type or write on yo
 ur photograph and correctly point out the specific elements. (You are welc
 ome to do more than four elements\, but four is the minimum requirement.)
 \n\nOption 2: Sketch a Building\n---------------------------\n\nIf you abs
 olutely cannot go out and visit a building and do not have a photo of your
 self in front of a building with Greek architectural features\, you can ch
 oose this option.\n\nStep 1: Select a Building\n-------------------------
 \n\nChoose a real\, identifiable building that has at least six Greek arch
 itectural features. Search for images of buildings suggested in the photo 
 option from your hometown\, downtown Provo\, or another location you've pe
 rsonally visited.\n\nStep 2: Create Your Sketch\n-------------------------
 -\n\nYour sketch\, which must be drawn with pen/pencil and paper or a digi
 tal drawing program (AI-generated sketches will receive 0 points) must:\n
 \n* Sketch one entire side of the building. You do not need to do a 3D ren
 dering of the whole building (unless that is your thing!)\, but you cannot
  sketch just part of one side. It needs to look like a full side of the bu
 ilding as if you were taking a photo in front of it. \n\n* Label and clea
 rly identify at least six identifiable Greek architectural elements.\n\nSt
 ep 3: Submit Your Work\n------------------------\n\n* Submit a clear photo
 graph or PDF of your labeled sketch.\n\n* Be sure to include the building
 ’s name and location. \n\nYou may identify any of the following element
 s. See the required number in your instructions above.\n\n* Pediment\n\n* 
 Doric capital\n\n* Ionic capital\n\n* Stylobate\n\n* Entablature\n\n* Frie
 ze\n\n* Cornice\n\n* Raking cornice\n\n* Fluted columns\n\n* Triglyph\n\n*
  Metope\n\nTip: Buildings with one Greek architectural element often inclu
 de several others\, so finding four or six elements may be easier than you
  expect if you look closely. \n\nWhat to Submit\n--------------\n\nBefore
  you submit your labeled photo or sketch as a JPEG\, PNG\, or PDF\, comple
 te the checklist for your option.\n\nPhotograph Checklist\n---------------
 -----\n\n* I am visible in front of the building.\n\n* The architectural f
 eatures are visible.\n\n* I included the building’s name and location.\n
 \n* I identified at least four Greek architectural elements.\n\nSketch Che
 cklist\n----------------\n\n* I sketched the entire building.\n\n* The bui
 lding is real and identifiable.\n\n* I included the building’s name and 
 location.\n\n* I identified at least six Greek architectural elements.\n\n
 * I submitted a clear photograph of my sketch.\n\nModule Item Completion (
 browser only)
