 -top: 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35px 30
 px\; font-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;"><strong>Instructions</
 strong></h3>\n<p>Choose one of the following ways to complete this assignm
 ent.</p>\n<div class="dp-panels-wrapper dp-accordion-default dp-panel-acti
 ve-color-dp-accent dp-panel-heading-p-1">\n<div class="dp-panel-group">\n<
 h3 class="dp-panel-heading" style="background-color: #e5efeb\;">Option 1: 
 Visit a Building (preferred option)</h3>\n<div class="dp-panel-content">\n
 <h4 id="greek-architecture" class="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-prim
 ary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 20px\; font-size: 18px\; margin-botto
 m: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Step 1: Find a Building</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr
 -solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-color: #eeeeee\; colo
 r: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 20px\;">\n<p>Look for a buil
 ding with at least <strong>four</strong> Greek architectural elements from
  the list below.</p>\n<p>Good places to search include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Uni
 versities</li>\n<li>Government buildings</li>\n<li>Theaters</li>\n<li>Bank
 s</li>\n<li>Museums</li>\n<li>Libraries</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id="greek-archite
 cture" class="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" sty
 le="margin-top: 50px\; font-size: 18px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005
 a38\;">Step 2: Take a Photograph</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-mar
 gin-direction-tblr" style="border-color: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin
 -top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 20px\;">\n<p>Take a photograph that:</p>\n<ul>
 \n<li>Shows you standing in front of the building</li>\n<li>Clearly shows 
 the architectural elements you plan to identify</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Selfies ar
 e welcome\, but you need to be able to see the architectural element. Cons
 ider bringing a friend or family member and sharing what you've learned wi
 th them. They will be so impressed with your architectural knowledge. You 
 may use a photograph from a previous trip or occasion\, but you <strong>mu
 st</strong> be in the photo. Finding a building during the current term is
  encouraged!</p>\n<h4 id="greek-architecture" class="dp-margin-direction-t
 blr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 50px\; font-size: 1
 8px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Step 3: Submit Your Work</h4
 >\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-co
 lor: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 20px\;">
 \n<p>Submit the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your photograph</li>\n<li>The bu
 ilding’s name and location</li>\n<li>Four clearly identified Greek archi
 tectural elements visible in the photograph--type or write on your photogr
 aph and correctly point out the specific elements. (You are welcome to do 
 more than four elements\, but four is the minimum requirement.)</li>\n</ul
 >\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-panel-group">\n<h3 class="dp-panel-headi
 ng" style="background-color: #e5efeb\;">Option 2: Sketch a Building</h3>\n
 <div class="dp-panel-content">\n<p>If you absolutely cannot go out and vis
 it a building and do not have a photo of yourself in front of a building w
 ith Greek architectural features\, you can choose this option.</p>\n<h4 id
 ="greek-architecture" class="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp
 -text-bold" style="margin-top: 20px\; font-size: 18px\; margin-bottom: 10p
 x\; color: #005a38\;">Step 1: Select a Building</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-sol
 id-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-color: #eeeeee\; color: #
 c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 20px\;">\n<p>Choose a real\, ide
 ntifiable building that has at least <strong>six</strong> Greek architectu
 ral features. Search for images of buildings suggested in the photo option
  from your hometown\, downtown Provo\, or another location you've personal
 ly visited.</p>\n<h4 id="greek-architecture" class="dp-margin-direction-tb
 lr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 50px\; font-size: 18
 px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Step 2: Create Your Sketch</h
 4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-c
 olor: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 20px\;">
 \n<p>Your sketch\, which must be drawn with pen/pencil and paper or a digi
 tal drawing program (AI-generated sketches will receive 0 points) must:</p
 >\n<ul>\n<li>Sketch one entire side of the building. You do not need to do
  a 3D rendering of the whole building (unless that is your thing!)\, but y
 ou cannot sketch just part of one side. It needs to look like a full side 
 of the building as if you were taking a photo in front of it.&nbsp\;</li>
 \n<li>Label and clearly identify at least <strong>six</strong> identifiabl
 e Greek architectural elements.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id="greek-architecture" c
 lass="dp-margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="marg
 in-top: 50px\; font-size: 18px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">S
