 \nLesson 4 Mini-Concept Check: Classical Greece and Hellenistic\n---------
 -----------------------------------------------------\n\nIn this quiz\, yo
 u will focus on concepts from this lesson. The open-book nature lets you k
 now which concepts to study so you are better prepared for the concepts co
 vered in the upcoming exams.\n\nInstructions\n------------\n\nThis multipl
 e-choice quiz draws from a large question bank\, so each attempt may inclu
 de questions you have not seen before.\n\nTo prepare\, review:\n\n* Learni
 ng Outcomes on the overview page\n\n* The “Terms to Track” and “Peop
 le to Track” sections at the lesson pages\n\nYou may retake the quiz as 
 many times as needed. For the best preparation\, continue taking it until 
 you have encountered every question in the question bank. Unit Checks draw
  from a similar bank\, so the more questions you encounter and review now
 \, the better prepared you will be.\n\nRules\n-----\n\nThe quiz consists o
 f the following rules.\n\n* Open book and note (so you can know what conce
 pts to focus on for the exams)\n\n* Unlimited attempts\n\n* No time limit
 \n\n* Your highest score will be kept\n\nIf taking this quiz again after t
 he due date\, use the practice quiz below.\n\nUsing the Quiz for Exam Revi
 ew\n------------------------------\n\nAfter the due date\, use [Mini-Conce
 pt Check: Classical Greece and Hellenisitic (Practice)] (https://byu.instr
 ucture.com/courses/36390/quizzes/656508) to review for the exam. It contai
 ns the same questions and can be taken late without affecting this score. 
 No points are associated with the practice version of this quiz.\n\nModule
  Item Completion (browser only)
