 son 4 Mini-ID Check: Classical Greece and Hellenistic\n-------------------
 --------------------------------------\n\nIn this quiz\, you will identify
  the names\, eras\, and other identifying factors of various artworks you 
 learned about in this lesson. This quiz will cover the following eras.\n\n
 * Classical\n\n* Late Classical\n\n* Hellenistic\n\nWhat to Expect\n------
 --------\n\nEach identification question will ask you to identify the foll
 owing about each piece.\n\n* Name\n\n* Era\n\n* Artist (if known)\n\nNot a
 ll artwork in the lesson will appear here. See the artwork listed in the I
 mages to Identify section at the top of the lesson pages to best prepare.
 \n\nQuiz Rules\n----------\n\nThe quiz consists of the following rules.\n
 \n* Open book and note\n\n* No time limit\n\n* Unlimited attempts\n\n* You
 r highest score will be kept\n\n* If taking this quiz for a second time af
 ter the due date\, use the practice quiz below\n\n​\n\nWhat is the point
  of this quiz?\n-------------------------------\n\nThese Mini-ID Checks ar
 e designed to be practice for the Unit Checks\, which cover multiple lesso
 ns.\n\nTake this quiz as many times as needed to prepare for the upcoming 
 Unit Check\, since the main Unit Checks will pull from the artwork covered
  in these quizzes.\n\nUsing the Quiz for Exam Review\n--------------------
 ----------\n\nAfter the due date\, use [Mini-ID Check: Classical Greece an
 d Hellenistic (Practice)] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/36390/quiz
 zes/654389) to review for the exam. It contains the same questions and can
  be taken late without affecting your Mini-ID Check: Classical Greece and 
 Hellenistic. No points are associated with the practice version of this qu
 iz.\n\nModule Item Completion (browser only)
