BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Who Owns the Parthenon Sculptures? Reply to Topic [IHUM 201-022]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260919
DTSTAMP:20260905T004300Z
UID:event-sub-assignment-1466312
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:-------------------------------------------\nLesson 4 Who Owns
  the Parthenon Sculptures?\n-------------------------------------------\n
 \nAs alluded to in the video on the last page\, the ownership of much of t
 he sculpture of the Parthenon is a matter of controversy.\n\nOn this page
 \, you will consider both sides of the argument and share your thoughts on
  the subject with your small group. \n\nSee Both Sides\n--------------\n
 \nWatch the following video. Take a minute to “think charitably” about
  this topic. Can you see both sides of the argument? What further question
 s do you have?\n\nNote: if you need a refresher on what it means to "think
  charitably\," return to the Hank Green video on the [Presocratic Philosop
 hy] (LINK.PLACEHOLDER_8b125d239407f7d4f089eb044092846f) page.\n\nTranscrip
 t: Forthcoming\n\nPost Video Response\n-------------------\n\nAfter watchi
 ng Who Owns the Parthenon Sculptures?\, consider the arguments presented i
 n the video. Should the sculptures remain in the British Museum\, or shoul
 d they be returned to Athens?\n\nRecord and post a 1-2 minute video for yo
 ur small group in which you:\n\n* State which position you support.\n\n* E
 xplain why\, using at least one example of supporting evidence from the vi
 deo as well as your own thought and feelings from personal experience.\n\n
 * Briefly acknowledge one reason someone might support the other position.
 \n\nYour goal here is not to "win" an argument but to share your perspecti
 ve thoughtfully and respectfully. It is okay to see value in both sides\, 
 but decide which position you support today. Your opinion may change in th
 e future as you gain more knowledge and experience and that is 100% okay\;
  this video simply captures what you think today.\n\nHow do I record a vid
 eo in my post?\n\nAfter you click Reply below\, complete the following ste
 ps to record your video.\n\n[Click Upload/Record Media after clicking Repl
 y. Don't Attach a video.] (LINK.PLACEHOLDER_b3b447133ff29b4dbec2f8ac39e2ab
 2d)     \n\n[Click on the Record button instead of uploading a file fro
 m the computer.] (LINK.PLACEHOLDER_dca70a6f64f2597768189192bd07f73d)    
  \n\n[Click the Start Recording button] (LINK.PLACEHOLDER_6c38d6e42c979c5
 3b0ab719367430c66)     \n\nSince your classmates are relying on you to 
 post on time so they can respond\, late posts will not be accepted. \n\nM
 ake Two Comments\n-----------------\n\nWatch the videos posted by your gro
 up members and give a written response to at least two classmates.\n\nIn e
 ach response:\n\n* Identify a specific idea from their videos that stood o
 ut to you.\n\n* Explain whether that idea reinforced\, challenged\, or add
 ed to your own thinking.\n\n* Respond respectfully\, whether you agree or 
 disagree.\n\nThe goal is to show that you thoughtfully and respectfully co
 nsidered perspectives other than your own. A response needs to be much mor
 e than "Cool" or "I agree." It needs to show that you watched\, listened t
 o\, and thought about their point of view. You are welcome to ask further 
 questions and turn this into a conversation\, but your grade is based on y
 our first response. \n\nIn most careers\, your work depends on others. Le
 arning to wait\, plan ahead\, and follow through is a valuable professiona
 l skill. Therefore\, if you post your main video first or second\, set a r
 eminder to return and respond after two peers have posted.\n\nGrading\n---
 ----\n\nClick on the     button in the top right-hand corner to see th
 e Rubric.\n\nModule Item Completion (browser only)
