 \; color: #000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; border-color: #005a38\;">
 \n<h3 id="assignment-instructions" class="dp-border-dir-tblr dp-border-sty
 le-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border
 -width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; padding-top: 12p
 x\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35px 30px\; font
 -size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;"><strong>Instructions</strong></
 h3>\n<div class="dp-callout dp-callout-placeholder card dp-callout-positio
 n-default dp-callout-type-info dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-callout-color-w
 arning" style="margin-left: 45px\; margin-right: 45px\; margin-top: 35px\;
 ">\n<div class="dp-callout-side-emphasis"><i class="dp-icon dp-default-ico
 n fas fa-exclamation-triangle" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dp-icon-con
 tent" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i></div>\n<div class="card-b
 ody">\n<div class="card-title" style="font-size: 21px\;" role="heading" ar
 ia-level="4"><strong class="" style="font-size: 20px\;">Do This Yourself: 
 No Generative AI</strong></div>\n<p>This is just a reminder not to use Cha
 tGPT or another generative AI tool to brainstorm\, draft\, rewrite\, or re
 vise this assignment.</p>\n<p>AI might create a clever adaptation\, but <s
 trong>your</strong><strong>&nbsp\;creative choices are the assignment</str
 ong>. Deciding what the conflict means\, what motivates the characters\, a
 nd how the scene could happen today will help you better understand <em>An
 tigone</em>. If AI makes those decisions for you here\, that learning is l
 ost. You are creative! Trust yourself to come up with something unique and
  interesting!</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<h4 id="step-1-choose-scene" class="dp-
 margin-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 4
 5px\; font-size: 20px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Step 1: Ch
 oose It</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style
 ="border-color: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom
 : 20px\;">\n<p style="color: #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">Choose
  one short scene or exchange that interests you. Look for a clear conflict
  or turning point\; do not adapt the whole play.</p>\n<p style="color: #00
 0000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">Before you begin\, identify:</p>\n<ul 
 style="color: #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">\n<li>What does each 
 main character want\, and why?</li>\n<li>What power or choice does each ch
 aracter have?</li>\n<li>What key choice and consequence must remain?</li>
 \n<li>What modern situation creates a similar conflict?</li>\n</ul>\n<div 
 class="dp-panels-wrapper dp-accordion-default" style="color: #000000\; bac
 kground-color: #ffffff\;">\n<div class="dp-panel-group">\n<h3 class="dp-pa
 nel-heading">Need help choosing a scene?&nbsp\;</h3>\n<div class="dp-panel
 -content">\n<p>If you need help choosing a scene\, consider one of the fol
 lowing that fits the assignment requirements. This list is not comprehensi
 ve\; you can choose a scene not included here.</p>\n<ul style="list-style-
 type: disc\;">\n<li>Antigone asks Ismene to help bury Polyneices\; Ismene 
 refuses (pgs. 3-8).&nbsp\;</li>\n<li>The Guard reports the burial\; Creon 
 accuses and threatens him (pgs. 15–20).</li>\n<li>The Guard brings in An
 tigone and explains how she was caught (pgs. 21–24).</li>\n<li>Creon que
 stions Antigone\; she defends breaking his law (pgs. 25–29).</li>\n<li>I
 smene tries to share Antigone’s guilt\; Antigone rejects her claim (pgs.
  29–33).</li>\n<li>Haemon tries to reason with Creon\; their disagreemen
 t becomes a confrontation (pgs. 34–41).</li>\n<li>Antigone faces her pun
 ishment and argues with the Chorus and Creon (pgs. 42–48).</li>\n<li>Tir
 esias warns Creon\; Creon refuses to listen and attacks his motives (pgs. 
 50–56).</li>\n<li>The Messenger tells Eurydice what happened to Antigone
  and Haemon (pgs. 59–64).</li>\n<li>Creon returns and learns the full co
 nsequences of his decisions (pgs. 64–68).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<
 /div>\n<h4 id="step-2-modernize-setting" class="dp-margin-direction-tblr c
 p-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 50px\; font-size: 20px\;
  margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Step 2: Move It to the Modern Wor
 ld</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="bor
 der-color: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bottom: 20p
 x\;">\n<p style="color: #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">Move the sc
 ene to a specific modern setting. It might take place in a family\, school
 \, workplace\, government\, community\, or any other setting you want.</p>
 \n<p style="color: #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">You may update:<
 /p>\n<ul style="color: #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">\n<li>Charac
 ter names (though you don't have to)</li>\n<li>Places and occupations</li>
 \n<li>Objects and customs</li>\n<li>Social and cultural references</li>\n<
 li>Consequence type (but still keep the level of seriousness the same)</li
 >\n</ul>\n<p style="color: #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">Preserve
  the original conflict\, motivations\, power relationships\, and key choic
 es. Keep the characters complex\; do not turn one side into a simple hero 
 or villain.</p>\n<blockquote class="dp-border-style-solid dp-margin-direct
 ion-tblr" style="background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-left-
 color: #f1c232\; border-top-width: 0px\; margin-top: 25px\; border-bottom-
 width: 0px\; border-right-width: 0px\;">\n<p>Note: <em>Antigone</em> inclu
 des death\, suicide\, grief\, family trauma\, and state violence. You do n
 ot need to recreate these events explicitly. You may keep serious events o
 ffstage or non-graphic\, use another serious consequence\, or choose anoth
 er passage.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h4 id="step-3-write-scene" class="dp-marg
 in-direction-tblr cp-txt-dp-primary dp-text-bold" style="margin-top: 50px
 \; font-size: 20px\; margin-bottom: 10px\; color: #005a38\;">Step 3: Write
  the Scene</h4>\n<hr class="dp-hr-solid-light dp-margin-direction-tblr" st
 yle="border-color: #eeeeee\; color: #c7c9c7\; margin-top: 8px\; margin-bot
 tom: 20px\;">\n<p style="color: #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">Rec
 reate the scene in clear\, contemporary language while keeping it in scrip
 t format. Label each speaker and include brief stage directions when neede
 d. Greek tragedies often used poetic meters such as <strong><a id="dpPopup
 0" class="dp-popover-trigger" href="#dpPopup0Content" aria-describedby="#d
 pPopup0Content">iambic trimeter</a></strong>\, but you do not need to use 
 poetic meter. Write natural dialogue—the way you speak or imagine your c
 haracters would speak today.</p>\n<p style="color: #000000\; background-co
 lor: #ffffff\;">Use the “roommate test”: If you can hand the script to
  your roommates and they can perform the scene without asking who says eac
 h line or what is happening\, your script is clear and correctly formatted
 .</p>\n<div id="dpPopup0Content" class="dp-popover-content dp-popup-conten
 t" style="background: #f7f7f7\; padding: 10px\; width: 600px\; max-width: 
 100%\; margin: auto\; border-radius: 3px\; border: 1px solid #a9a9a9\;">\n
 <p>Three feet of iambic meter\, which consists of an unstressed syllable f
 ollowed by a stressed syllable.</p>\n</div>\n<p style="color: #000000\; ba
 ckground-color: #ffffff\;">Your adaptation should:</p>\n<ul style="color: 
 #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">\n<li>Have a clear beginning\, midd
 le\, and end.</li>\n<li>Use a specific and consistent modern setting.</li>
 \n<li>Show the characters’ key choices and consequences.</li>\n<li>Show 
 what happens instead of simply summarizing it (be in script format).</li>
 \n</ul>\n<p style="color: #000000\; background-color: #ffffff\;">Your adap
 tation does not need to be the same length as the original scene. As long 
 as you capture the above requirements in a thoughtful way\, any length is 
 acceptable.</p>\n<p>Below is an example of a modernized scene. We’ve put
  it in a drop-down because you do not need to read this if you don’t wan
 t it to influence your own idea. It will give you a possible way to approa
 ch this\, but it is just one possibility. Have fun with this project! Let 
 your creativity flow! Your writing style will be different because you hav
 e your own unique experiences\, perspectives\, and voice.</p>\n<div class=
 "dp-panels-wrapper dp-accordion-default dp-panel-color-dp-accent">\n<div c
 lass="dp-panel-group">\n<h3 class="dp-panel-heading">Great Example of a Mo
 dernized Scene&nbsp\;</h3>\n<div class="dp-panel-content">\n<blockquote st
 yle="border-left-color: #cc0000\;">\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> This exampl
 e models one possible approach. You can still modernize the same scene\, b
 ut do not reuse the setting or specific situation in your own adaptation.<
 /p>\n</blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level="1">\n<strong>Scene: </strong>Lin
 es 1-97</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level="1">\n<strong>Modern Location</s
 trong>: High School&nbsp\;</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level="1">\n<strong
 >Title: </strong>“Stick it to the Man”</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>After schoo
 l. Ismene sits on her bed\, scrolling through her phone. Antigone rushes i
 nto the room.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> Sis! Can you b
 elieve what an idiot that superintendent Creon is?&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><
 strong>Ismene:</strong><span> I really haven’t heard anything since Poly
 neices and Eteocles went off to college. I miss them so much. I’ve kinda
  been out of it.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> Ye
 ah\, I noticed. You good?&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Ismene:</strong><s
 pan> It’s whatever\, just spill it.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigo
 ne:</strong><span> Okay\, so Polyneices and Eteocles just broke track and 
 field state records at that track meet\, right? Amazing\, cream of the cro
 p\, rising freshman. Great. Creon just put a display case in the district 
 athletic building\, and get this. He only put up Eteocles! Can you believe
  that? It’s such baloney! He says it’s cause Polyneices went to Bull R
 un High. Bull Run High had that cheating scandal\, but they never proved P
 olyneices did anything. And as if that wasn’t enough\, he said whoever p
 uts Polyneices’ posters around\, wears t-shirts\, or does anything to su
 pport him is gonna get expelled. It’s up to you and me to make sure Poly
 neices gets the credit he deserves.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>I
 smene:</strong><span> I’m not sure that’s the best idea.&nbsp\;</span>
 </p>\n<p><strong>Antigone: </strong><span>Listen\, none of this back and f
 orth\, okay? Are you in or out?</span></p>\n<p><strong>Ismene:</strong><sp
 an> What are you planning on doing?&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone
 :</strong><span> I’m gonna break into the district building tonight\, de
 corate the display for Polyneices\, and trash Creon’s office.&nbsp\;</sp
 an></p>\n<p><strong>Ismene:</strong><span> <em>Stands in alarm.</em> Are y
 ou crazy?&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> Polyneice
 s is our brother. It’s not fair he doesn’t get a place on that display
  case. He deserves it. I’m gonna show Creon who’s boss.&nbsp\;</span><
 /p>\n<p><strong>Ismene:</strong><span> But you’re gonna get in big troub
 le!&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> I don’t care.
  Everyone knows it’s the right thing to do.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><stron
 g>Ismene:</strong><span> Antigone. I know you’re trying to do what’s b
 est for our family\, but the truth is everyone in our small town already k
 nows how sketchy our family’s past is. It’s just us here now\, and we 
 get somewhat of a fresh start. I don’t think we should be messing around
 .&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> <em>Grabs her bac
 kpack. </em>Fine\, forget it. I’ll do it myself. I’m going to make my 
 big brother proud.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Ismene</strong><span>: Listen\, 
 I love Polyneices\, but it’s not worth risking our futures and getting e
 xpelled.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> Excuses\, excuses
 . It’s fine\, like I said\, I’ll do it myself.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><
 strong>Ismene:</strong><span> Antigone\, please don’t do this.&nbsp\;</s
 pan></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> Don’t worry about it. I’
 m not gonna get caught.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Ismene:</strong><span> Just
  don’t tell anyone else about it. I’ll keep it on the down low also.&n
 bsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> Girl\, shout it out 
 to the rooftops for all I care. Come on\, live a little!</span></p>\n<p><s
 trong>Ismene: </strong><span>You’re such a martyr\, Antigone.&nbsp\;</sp
 an></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> What can I say? I live for th
 e applause.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Ismene:</strong><span> Only if y
 ou don’t get caught.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone: </strong><e
 m>Holds up her phone.</em><strong> </strong><span>When I do get caught\, t
 he deed will already be done. I’m posting it.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><str
 ong>Ismene:</strong><span> Why even try it if you’re gonna get caught?&n
 bsp\;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Antigone:</strong><span> My mind’s made up.
  Full send. Both our brothers deserve the best.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Ism
 ene</strong><span>: Do what you want then. You’ll still be the most popu
 lar girl in school.</span></p>\n<p><em>Antigone exits. Ismene watches her 
 leave\, worried.</em></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-panel-group">\n<
 h3 class="dp-panel-heading">Poor Example of a Modernized Scene</h3>\n<div 
 class="dp-panel-content">\n<p>"I chose the scene where Creon questions Ant
 igone after she breaks his law. My adaptation takes place at a modern high
  school. Antigone is a student named Anna\, and Creon is the principal\, M
 r. Carter.</p>\n<p>Anna’s brother had been suspended for getting into a 
 fight. Mr. Carter told everyone that students were not allowed to talk to 
 him or help him with schoolwork because he needed to learn his lesson. Ann
 a thought this was unfair\, so she secretly brought her brother his homewo
 rk. Another student saw her and reported her to the principal.</p>\n<p>Mr.
  Carter called Anna into his office and asked why she had broken the rule.
  Anna said that family was more important than school rules. Mr. Carter be
 came angry because he believed students should always obey the principal. 
 Anna refused to apologize\, so he suspended her. She left the office feeli
 ng proud of herself\, while Mr. Carter went back to work."</p>\n<blockquot
 e style="border-left-color: #cc0000\;">\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> This is
  a weak example because it summarizes the encounter instead of showing it
 \, does not use script format\, makes the conflict too simple\, and gives 
 the characters little depth. The modern consequence also does not carry th
 e same seriousness as the choice in <em>Antigone</em>.</p>\n</blockquote>
 \n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block dp-margin-d
 irection-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-shadow-b1 dp-border-dir-none" s
 tyle="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 0px 35px 25px\; background-color: 
 #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; border-color: #005a
 38\;">\n<h3 id="what-to-submit-modern-antigone" class="dp-border-dir-tblr 
 dp-border-style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" 
 style="border-width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; pad
 ding-top: 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35p
 x 30px\; font-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;"><strong>What to Su
 bmit</strong></h3>\n<p>You will submit two items on this page</p>\n<ol>\n<
 li>Your modernized scene as a DOCX or PDF file. Your file should include:
 \n<ul style="list-style-type: disc\;">\n<li>Original scene line numbers</l
 i>\n<li>Modern setting location</li>\n<li>Title of your adaptation</li>\n<
 li>Script of scene</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<span data-olk-copy-source="M
 essageBody">Statement in the submission comment box saying\, "This is all 
 my own work\, and I didn't use AI."</span>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-olk-copy-
 source="MessageBody">If this statement is not true\, please redo this assi
 gnment using your own work before you submit it.</span></li>\n<li><span da
 ta-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">If this statement is not included in the 
 submission comment\, the assignment will not be graded.</span></li>\n</ul>
 \n</li>\n</ol>\n<blockquote class="dp-border-style-solid dp-margin-directi
 on-tblr" style="background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-left-c
 olor: #f1c232\; border-top-width: 0px\; margin-top: 25px\; border-bottom-w
 idth: 0px\; border-right-width: 0px\;">\n<p>Note: you must submit your ann
 otations (Part 1) on the previous page before your modern adaptation (Part
  2) will be graded.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-blo
 ck dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="padding: 20p
 x 25px\; background-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin-top: 55px\; m
 argin-bottom: 0px\;">\n<div class="dp-progress-placeholder dp-module-progr
 ess-completion dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="display: none\; background
 -color: #eeeeee\; color: #000000\;">Module Item Completion (browser only)<
 /div>\n</div>\n</div><script src="https://instructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws
