BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Socratic Inquiry: Map or Reflection [IHUM 201-022]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTSTAMP:20260901T180800Z
UID:event-assignment-1466363
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:--------------------------------------------\nLesson 6 Socrati
 c Inquiry: Map or Reflection\n--------------------------------------------
 \n\nFor this activity\, you will use Socratic questioning to explore the i
 ntellectual virtue you selected earlier in the course. You will question y
 our own ideas\, talk with two other people\, and then show where those con
 versations took your thinking.\n\nThis activity has three parts:\n\n* Thin
 k: Question your own ideas about the virtue.\n\n* Talk: Explore the virtue
  with at least two other people.\n\n* Create: Share what you discovered in
  a mind map or written reflection.\n\nYou do not need to arrive at one per
 fect definition. Discovering that a virtue is more complicated than you fi
 rst thought is part of the activity.\n\nStep 1: Question Yourself\n-------
 ------------------\n\nBegin with the [intellectual virtue] (#dpPopup0Conte
 nt) you selected earlier in the course:\n\nCuriosity • Autonomy  • H
 umility  • Attentiveness • Carefulness • Thoroughness • Open-mind
 edness • Courage • Tenacity\n\nWrite down your own questions and thoug
 hts about your virtue. You might begin with:\n\n* What does this virtue me
 an to me?\n\n* When is it helpful?\n\n* Can it ever be misused?\n\n* What 
 might too much or too little of it look like?\n\n* Where does it matter ou
 tside school?\n\n* When have I seen someone practice it?\n\nLet one questi
 on lead to another. Keep notes so you can use them later.\n\n   Try this
 :\n\nTimer method: Set a 15-minute timer and write down everything that co
 mes to mind. This is called a brain dump. Write as much as possible during
  those fifteen minutes. Some of it will be interesting and useful and some
  of it won't. That's normal. You can sift through your thoughts and see wh
 at further ideas and questions you have. \n\nRuminating method: You might
  not be a brain dump person. It is also okay to contemplate the virtue thr
 oughout the day or several days and record ideas as they occur to you. Kee
 p a notepad close or make a dedicated note in your phone so that you can a
 dd thoughts as they come to you. \n\n​\n\nDo This One Yourself: No Gene
 rative AI\n--------------------------------------\n\nChatting with an AI b
 ot is not the same as having a conversation with yourself. This needs to b
 e you thinking about the virtue on your own. The goal is to find out what 
 you think about it\, not what a large language model thinks. Please do not
  chat with AI for this assignment.\n\nStep 2: Question Other People\n-----
 ------------------------\n\nTalk with at least two living people about you
 r chosen virtue.\n\nIf possible\, choose at least one person whose age\, e
 xperience\, or life situation differs from yours. This could be a grandpar
 ent\, parent\, supervisor\, professor\, neighbor\, or another person you r
 espect.\n\nBegin with a simple question\, such as “What does courage mea
 n to you?” Then ask follow-up questions:\n\n* Why do you define it that 
 way?\n\n* Can you give me an example?\n\n* Is this virtue always helpful?
 \n\n* Can someone take it too far?\n\n* Has your understanding of it chang
 ed over time or through a specific experience?\n\nLet the conversation dev
 elop naturally. Give the other person space to ask you questions\, too.\n
 \nYou may take notes during the conversation\, but if that is distracting 
 from being present in the conversation\, write them immediately afterward 
 so that they are fresh in your memory.\n\nStep 3: Show Where the Questions
  Led\n------------------------------------\n\nChoose one of the following 
 ways to submit what you learned.\n\nOption 1: Create a Mind Map or Thought
  Web\n------------------------------------------\n\nPlace your intellectua
 l virtue at the center. Build outward to show the questions\, answers\, ex
 amples\, disagreements\, and new insights that emerged.\n\nYour map must i
 nclude:\n\n* Your chosen virtue at the center\n\n* Ideas from your own que
 stioning\n\n* Specific details from both conversations\n\n* Connections am
 ong the three perspectives\n\n* Evidence of where your thinking changed or
  deepened\n\nCreating the map by hand will probably be easiest. You could 
 also go to the whiteboards in the [BYU Library Makerspace] (https://lib.by
 u.edu/services/makerspace/). Submit a clear\, readable photograph of the f
 inished map.\n\nIf you already use a digital mind-mapping program (or want
  to use something simple like the [whiteboard on Canva] (https://www.canva
 .com/online-whiteboard/templates/))\, tell your TA which program you used.
  Do not use an AI-generated map or an AI-powered mapping tool.\n\nOption 2
 : Written Reflection\n----------------------------\n\nWrite at least three
  full paragraphs explaining where your questioning led you.\n\nYour reflec
 tion must include:\n\n* Questions you asked yourself and others\n\n* Speci
 fic responses or insights from both conversations\n\n* Connections or diff
 erences among the three perspectives\n\n* How your perception of the virtu
 e has expanded\n\nUse your own thoughts\, ideas\, and words.\n\nAgain\, AI
 -generated writing is not acceptable in any form for this assignment. All 
 of the writing must be your own thoughts\, ideas\, and words. Do not use a
 ny AI checks such as Grammarly\, Gemini\, Copilot\, etc. to “fix” your
  writing. It needs to be wholly original and written by you.\n\nWhat to Su
 bmit\n--------------\n\nSubmit one of the following\, depending on which o
 ption you chose above.\n\n* Option 1: A clear photograph of your completed
  mind map or thought web\n\n* Option 2: A written reflection of at least 
 three full paragraphs\n\nModule Item Completion (browser only)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://byu.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _36390&month=09&year=2026#assignment_1466363
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instruct
 ure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8409020
 /dp_app.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructure-uploads.s3.a
 mazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8073295/canvas-byuonlin
 e-app.css"><div id="dp-wrapper" class="dp-wrapper" style="background-color
 : #f9f9f9\; color: #000000\; border-radius: 2px\;">\n<header class="dp-hea
 der dp-border-dir-tblr dp-border-style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-
 margin-direction-tblr" style="border-width: 8px 0px 0px\; padding-top: 0px
 \; padding-bottom: 0px\; margin-bottom: 0px\; border-radius: 2px\; padding
 -left: 7px\; border-color: #005a38\; background-color: #005a38\; color: #f
 fffff\;">\n<h2 id="page-title" class="dp-heading dp-margin-direction-tblr 
 dp-padding-direction-tblr" style="margin-top: 0px\; margin-bottom: 0px\; p
 adding-bottom: 20px\; padding-top: 18px\; padding-left: 5px\; border-color
 : #2b4226\; color: #ffffff\;">\n<span class="dp-header-pre dp-padding-dire
 ction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-text-bold dp-border-style-solid dp-
 border-dir-tblr" style="border-width: 0px 2px 0px 0px\; padding-right: 12p
 x\; background-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\;"><span class="dp-header-p
 re-1" style="color: #ffffff\;">Lesson 6</span></span> <span class="dp-head
 er-title dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr" style="margin
 -top: 0px\;">Socratic Inquiry: Map or Reflection</span>\n</h2>\n</header>
 \n<div class="dp-content-block dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-directi
 on-tblr dp-border-style-solid dp-border-dir-all dp-shadow-b1 lead" style="
 margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 25px 35px\; background-color: #ffffff\; 
 color: #000000\; border-width: 3px\; border-color: #005a38\;">\n<p class="
 lead" style="margin: 0 0 14px\;">For this activity\, you will use Socratic
  questioning to explore the intellectual virtue you selected earlier in th
 e course. You will question your own ideas\, talk with two other people\, 
 and then show where those conversations took your thinking.</p>\n<p class=
 "lead" style="margin: 0 0 14px\;">This activity has three parts:</p>\n<ul>
 \n<li>\n<strong>Think:</strong> Question your own ideas about the virtue.<
 /li>\n<li>\n<strong>Talk:</strong> Explore the virtue with at least two ot
 her people.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Create:</strong> Share what you discovered
  in a mind map or written reflection.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You do not need to a
 rrive at one perfect definition. Discovering that a virtue is more complic
 ated than you first thought is part of the activity.</p>\n</div>\n<div cla
 ss="dp-content-block dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp
 -shadow-b1 dp-border-dir-none" style="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 0p
 x 35px 25px\; background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-width: 5
 px 0px 0px\; border-color: #005a38\;">\n<h3 id="step-2-question-others" cl
 ass="dp-border-dir-tblr dp-border-style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp
 -margin-direction-tblr" style="border-width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; pa
 dding-bottom: 10px\; padding-top: 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #f
 fffff\; margin: 0px -35px 30px\; font-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a
 38\;"><strong>Step 1: Question Yourself</strong></h3>\n<p>Begin with the <
 a id="dpPopup0" class="dp-popover-trigger" href="#dpPopup0Content" aria-de
 scribedby="#dpPopup0Content">intellectual virtue</a>&nbsp\;you selected ea
 rlier in the course:</p>\n<div id="dpPopup0Content" class="dp-popover-cont
 ent dp-popup-content" style="background: #f7f7f7\; padding: 10px\; width: 
 600px\; max-width: 100%\; margin: auto\; border-radius: 3px\; border: 1px 
 solid #a9a9a9\;">\n<p>Curiosity • Autonomy &nbsp\;• Humility &nbsp\;
 • Attentiveness • Carefulness • Thoroughness • Open-mindedness •
  Courage • Tenacity</p>\n</div>\n<p>Write down your own questions and th
 oughts about your virtue. You might begin with:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>What does t
 his virtue mean to me?</li>\n<li>When is it helpful?</li>\n<li>Can it ever
  be misused?</li>\n<li>What might too much or too little of it look like?<
 /li>\n<li>Where does it matter outside school?</li>\n<li>When have I seen 
 someone practice it?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let one question lead to another. Kee
 p notes so you can use them later.</p>\n<blockquote class="dp-margin-direc
 tion-tblr" style="background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; margin-top:
  16px\; border-left-color: #ffffff\;">\n<p><strong><i class="dp-icon fas f
 a-lightbulb" style="color: #005a38\;" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dp-i
 con-content" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i>&nbsp\; Try this:</
 strong></p>\n<p>Timer method: Set a 15-minute timer and write down everyth
 ing that comes to mind. This is called a brain dump. Write as much as poss
 ible during those fifteen minutes. Some of it will be interesting and usef
 ul and some of it won't. That's normal. You can sift through your thoughts
  and see what further ideas and questions you have.&nbsp\;</p>\n<p>Ruminat
 ing method: You might not be a brain dump person. It is also okay to conte
 mplate the virtue throughout the day or several days and record ideas as t
 hey occur to you. Keep a notepad close or make a dedicated note in your ph
 one so that you can add thoughts as they come to you.&nbsp\;</p>\n</blockq
 uote>\n<div class="dp-callout dp-callout-placeholder card dp-callout-posit
 ion-default dp-callout-type-info dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-callout-color
 -warning" style="margin-left: 45px\; margin-right: 45px\; margin-top: 35px
 \;">\n<div class="dp-callout-side-emphasis"><i class="dp-icon dp-default-i
 con fas fa-exclamation-triangle">​</i></div>\n<div class="card-body">\n<
 h4 class="card-title" style="font-size: 21px\;">Do This One Yourself: No G
 enerative AI</h4>\n<p>Chatting with an AI bot is not the same as having a 
 conversation with yourself. This needs to be you thinking about the virtue
  on your own. The goal is to find out what you think about it\, not what a
  large language model thinks. Please<strong> do not</strong> chat with AI 
 for this assignment.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-b
 lock dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-shadow-b1 dp-bo
 rder-dir-none" style="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 0px 35px 25px\; ba
 ckground-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; bor
 der-color: #005a38\;">\n<h3 id="step-2-question-others" class="dp-border-d
 ir-tblr dp-border-style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-directio
 n-tblr" style="border-width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10
 px\; padding-top: 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 
 0px -35px 30px\; font-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;"><strong>St
 ep 2: Question Other People</strong></h3>\n<p>Talk with at least <strong>t
 wo living people</strong> about your chosen virtue.</p>\n<p>If possible\, 
 choose at least one person whose age\, experience\, or life situation diff
 ers from yours. This could be a grandparent\, parent\, supervisor\, profes
 sor\, neighbor\, or another person you respect.</p>\n<p>Begin with a simpl
 e question\, such as “What does courage mean to you?” Then ask follow-
 up questions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Why do you define it that way?</li>\n<li>Can 
 you give me an example?</li>\n<li>Is this virtue always helpful?</li>\n<li
 >Can someone take it too far?</li>\n<li>Has your understanding of it chang
 ed over time or through a specific experience?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let the con
 versation develop naturally. Give the other person space to ask you questi
 ons\, too.</p>\n<p>You may take notes during the conversation\, but if tha
 t is distracting from being present in the conversation\, write them immed
 iately afterward so that they are fresh in your memory.</p>\n</div>\n<div 
 class="dp-content-block dp-margin-direction-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr
  dp-shadow-b1 dp-border-dir-none" style="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding:
  0px 35px 25px\; background-color: #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-width
 : 5px 0px 0px\; border-color: #005a38\;">\n<h3 id="step-3-process-and-orga
 nize" class="dp-border-dir-tblr dp-border-style-solid dp-padding-direction
 -tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="border-width: 0px\; padding-left: 2
 2px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; padding-top: 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; c
 olor: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35px 30px\; font-size: 24px\; background-colo
 r: #005a38\;"><strong>Step 3: Show Where the Questions Led</strong></h3>\n
 <p>Choose one of the following ways to submit what you learned.</p>\n<div 
 class="dp-panels-wrapper dp-accordion-default dp-panel-active-color-dp-acc
 ent dp-panel-heading-p-1">\n<div class="dp-panel-group">\n<h3 class="dp-pa
 nel-heading" style="background-color: #e5efeb\;">\n<strong>Option 1</stron
 g>: Create a Mind Map or Thought Web</h3>\n<div class="dp-panel-content">
 \n<p>Place your intellectual virtue at the center. Build outward to show t
 he questions\, answers\, examples\, disagreements\, and new insights that 
 emerged.</p>\n<p>Your map must include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your chosen virtue 
 at the center</li>\n<li>Ideas from your own questioning</li>\n<li>Specific
  details from both conversations</li>\n<li>Connections among the three per
 spectives</li>\n<li>Evidence of where your thinking changed or deepened</l
 i>\n</ul>\n<p>Creating the map by hand will probably be easiest. You could
  also go to the whiteboards in the <a href="https://lib.byu.edu/services/m
 akerspace/">BYU Library Makerspace</a>. Submit a clear\, readable photogra
 ph of the finished map.</p>\n<p>If you already use a digital mind-mapping 
 program (or want to use something simple like the <a href="https://www.can
 va.com/online-whiteboard/templates/">whiteboard on Canva</a>)\, tell your 
 TA which program you used. Do not use an AI-generated map or an AI-powered
  mapping tool.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-panel-group">\n<h3 clas
 s="dp-panel-heading" style="background-color: #e5efeb\;">\n<strong>Option 
 2</strong>: Written Reflection</h3>\n<div class="dp-panel-content">\n<p>Wr
 ite at least <strong>three full paragraphs</strong> explaining where your 
 questioning led you.</p>\n<p>Your reflection must include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>
 Questions you asked yourself and others</li>\n<li>Specific responses or in
 sights from both conversations</li>\n<li>Connections or differences among 
 the three perspectives</li>\n<li>How your perception of the virtue has exp
 anded</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Use your own thoughts\, ideas\, and words.</p>\n<p>A
 gain\, AI-generated writing is not acceptable in any form for this assignm
 ent. All of the writing must be your own thoughts\, ideas\, and words. Do 
 not use any AI checks such as Grammarly\, Gemini\, Copilot\, etc. to “fi
 x” your writing. It needs to be wholly original and written by you.</p>
 \n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block dp-margin-d
 irection-tblr dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-shadow-b1 dp-border-dir-none" s
 tyle="margin: 50px 70px 40px\; padding: 0px 35px 25px\; background-color: 
 #ffffff\; color: #000000\; border-width: 5px 0px 0px\; border-color: #005a
 38\;">\n<h3 id="step-3-process-and-organize" class="dp-border-dir-tblr dp-
 border-style-solid dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" sty
 le="border-width: 0px\; padding-left: 22px\; padding-bottom: 10px\; paddin
 g-top: 12px\; border-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin: 0px -35px 3
 0px\; font-size: 24px\; background-color: #005a38\;"><strong>What to Submi
 t</strong></h3>\n<p>Submit one of the following\, depending on which optio
 n you chose above.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Option 1: A clear photograph of your com
 pleted mind map or thought web</li>\n<li>Option 2:&nbsp\;A written reflect
 ion of at least three full paragraphs</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-
 content-block dp-padding-direction-tblr dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="p
 adding: 20px 25px\; background-color: #005a38\; color: #ffffff\; margin-to
 p: 55px\; margin-bottom: 0px\;">\n<div class="dp-progress-placeholder dp-m
 odule-progress-completion dp-margin-direction-tblr" style="display: none\;
  background-color: #eeeeee\; color: #000000\;">Module Item Completion (bro
 wser only)</div>\n</div>\n</div><script src="https://instructure-uploads.s
