BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Attend a Live Event (Extra Credit) [IHUM 201-022]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTSTAMP:20260830T222100Z
UID:event-assignment-1475749
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:---------------------------------\nExtra Credit Attend a Live 
 Event\n---------------------------------\n\nThis optional activity can inc
 rease your Unit Checks grade percentage by up to 1%.\n\nInstructions\n----
 --------\n\nAttend\n------\n\nAttend a live\, college- or professional-lev
 el arts event\, such as a concert\, play\, musical\, dance performance\, o
 r opera. BYU is always offering amazing performances with student artists 
 and visiting artists. You may browse the [BYU Arts calendar] (https://cale
 ndar.byu.edu/arts-entertainment) for upcoming performances\, but the event
  does not need to be held at BYU.\n\nDuring the performance\, pay attentio
 n to the music\, staging\, costumes\, performances\, and other artistic ch
 oices.\n\nImportant: The event must be at a college or professional level.
  Supporting your little sister at her kindergarten program or your little 
 brother at his middle school band concert is wonderful\, but it does not c
 ount for this activity.\n\nWrite\n-----\n\nAs with all writing assignments
  in this course\, AI cannot be used for any part of your submission. This 
 needs to be all your own thoughts from beginning to end.\n\nSubmit a minim
 um of two pages\, double-spaced\, 12-point font review that includes a des
 cription of the event and then a personal response to it. You may include 
 things such as: \n\n*\n\nIn what time period was the play written/music c
 omposed/dance choreographed? Does the performance hearken back to any time
  period we have studied—where do you see this\, how is done\, and what i
 mplications does that have on your broader understanding of this work of a
 rt?\n\n* What specific artistic choices did the director/performer make an
 d what effect do they have?\n\n* What was the setting and how did it enhan
 ce/detract from the performance?\n\n* How did the audience respond?\n\n* W
 hat was your personal response in the moment and later when you thought ab
 out it more? (This needs to be more than "I liked it." Talk about the art 
 in detail. This should be a practice using the language of art to talk abo
 ut a performance.)\n\nWhat to Submit\n--------------\n\nSubmit your two-pa
 ge write-up as a DOCX or PDF file on this page.\n\nModule Item Completion 
 (browser only)
