SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:----------------------------\nExtra Credit Visit a Museum\n---
 -------------------------\n\nThis optional activity can increase your Unit
  Checks grade percentage by up to 1%.\n\nInstructions\n------------\n\nVis
 it a Museum\n--------------\n\nVisit a local museum with a physical notebo
 ok. Spend at least 30 minutes walking through the museum and becoming fami
 liar with the art on display. Notice which works capture your attention\, 
 and then complete the following steps.\n\n* Observe. Return to one artwork
  that especially interests you and spend at least 15 minutes with it. Do n
 ot use your phone or look up information online. Examine the artwork close
 ly from different angles and distances\, paying attention to its colors\, 
 materials\, details\, composition\, and overall effect. You may sketch the
  work or one of its details.\n\n* Reflect. Record your observations\, ques
 tions\, and personal reactions in your notebook. Then read the museum’s 
 description of the artwork and any printed information about the artist\, 
 adding relevant discoveries to your notes.\n\n* Research. Only after docum
 enting your firsthand experience should you use the internet to learn more
  about the artwork or artist. Use your observations and research to comple
 te the next part of the assignment.\n\nWrite\n-----\n\nWrite a review of a
 t least two full pages\, double-spaced\, in 12-point font. Begin with a de
 tailed description and analysis of the artwork\, then discuss your persona
 l response to it.\n\nAs you develop your review\, consider the following q
 uestions:\n\n* When was the artwork created? If it is more modern than the
  works studied in class\, what influences from earlier periods do you noti
 ce?\n\n* What choices did the artist make with light\, color\, shape\, mat
 erials\, composition\, or other formal elements? What effects do these cho
 ices create?\n\n* Does the artwork tell a story? If so\, how?\n\n* How is 
 the artwork displayed\, and how does the display affect your experience of
  it? Is it shown with similar works\, as part of a larger collection of th
 e artist’s work\, or on its own?\n\n* What was your response when you fi
 rst saw the artwork? How did your response change as you spent more time w
 ith it and reflected on it later?\n\nYour personal response should go beyo
 nd stating whether you liked the artwork. Discuss specific details from th
 e artwork and explain how they shaped your experience and interpretation.
 \n\nWhat to Submit\n--------------\n\nSubmit both of the following:\n\n* A
  clear\, readable photo of your handwritten museum notes and any sketches 
 you created.\n\n* Your completed review of at least two full pages\, doubl
 e-spaced\, in 12-point font.\n\nYou should submit both in a DOCX or PDF fi
 le.\n\nModule Item Completion (browser only)
