SUMMARY:Visit UVU "Roots of Knowledge" (Extra Credit) [IHUM 201-022]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTSTAMP:20260903T183000Z
UID:event-assignment-1483072
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:--------------------------------------------\nExtra Credit Vis
 it UVU "Roots of Knowledge"\n--------------------------------------------
 \n\nThis optional activity can increase your Activities grade percentage b
 y up to 1%.\n\nInstructions\n------------\n\n[] (https://byu.instructure.c
 om/courses/36390/files/13621345/preview?hidden=1)Visit\n------------------
 -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFor t
 hose of us in Utah\, Utah Valley University (UVU) has a stained glass wind
 ow exhibition in the Bingham Gallery of the Fulton Library. Admittance is 
 free\, and hours and directions can be found at [Roots of KnowledgeLinks 
 to an external site.] (https://www.uvu.edu/rootsofknowledge/). \n\nGrab a
  physical notebook and a pen or pencil for this assignment. Spend at least
  20 minutes walking through the museum and becoming familiar with the art 
 on display. This is not a quick walk-through. Before reading any written i
 nformation about the exhibit. Spend time with the installation--you\, your
  eyes\, your senses. Pay attention to which sections capture your attentio
 n\, and then complete the following steps.\n\n* Observe. Return to the sec
 tion that especially interests you and spend at least at least 10 more min
 utes with it. Do not use your phone or look up information online. Examine
  the artwork closely from different angles and distances\, paying attentio
 n to its colors\, details\, composition\, and overall effect. In your note
 book\, sketch the section you have decided to analyze OR take a selfie of 
 you with the section AND a cropped photo of the specific section you have 
 been analyzing. (You will submit either a photo of the sketch OR the selfi
 e and detail photo.)\n\n* Reflect. Record your personal observations\, que
 stions\, and personal reactions in your notebook. (You will submit a photo
  of these notes). After you have had your own experience with the art\, th
 en read the exhibit's description of the artwork and any printed informati
 on about the artist\, adding relevant discoveries to your notes.\n\n* Rese
 arch. Only after documenting your firsthand experience should you use the 
 internet to learn more about the artwork or artist. Use your observations 
 and research to complete the next part of the assignment.\n\nImportant: Yo
 u must go in person\; you cannot just view images online.\n\nWrite\n-----
 \n\nWrite a review of at least two full pages\, double-spaced\, in 12-poin
 t font. Begin with a detailed description and analysis of the artwork as w
 hole\, then the specific section you have analyzed\, then discuss your per
 sonal response to it.\n\nAs you develop your review\, consider the followi
 ng questions to help guide your review:\n\n* This is a contemporary work o
 f art\, but what influences from earlier periods do you notice?\n\n* What 
 choices did the artist make with light\, color\, shape\, materials\, compo
 sition\, or other formal elements? What effects do these choices create?\n
 \n* What story does the artwork as a whole and the specific section you de
 cided to analyze? How?\n\n* How does the way the artwork is displayed affe
 ct your experience of it? \n\n* What was your response when you first saw
  the artwork? How did your response change as you spent more time with it 
 and reflected on it later?\n\nYour personal response should go well beyond
  stating whether you liked the artwork. Discuss specific details from the 
 artwork and explain how they shaped your experience and interpretation.\n
 \nWhat to Submit\n--------------\n\nSubmit both of the following:\n\n* A c
 lear\, readable photo of your handwritten museum notes and sketch you crea
 ted OR the following 3 images: your handwritten notes AND a selfie photo A
 ND a detail photo.\n\n* Your completed review of at least two full pages\,
  double-spaced\, in 12-point font.\n\nYou should submit both in a DOCX or 
 PDF file.\n\nModule Item Completion (browser only)
